From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SableOS <noreply@sableos.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] SableOS: no hiss on the Q25 headphone jack

The MT6366 codec (mt6358.c) keeps the headphone amp gain in
ana_gain[HPOUTL/R], which starts at zero: DL_GAIN_8DB, +8 dB. Each
headphone power-up ramps the amp from -40 dB to that value. The stock
firmware writes "Headset Volume" 9 9 (DL_GAIN_N_1DB, -1 dB) for every
headphone stream; LineageOS and SableOS write nothing, so the amp runs
9 dB hot and the analog noise floor is heard as hiss.

Start ana_gain for both headphone channels at DL_GAIN_N_1DB when the
codec probes, so every power-up uses the stock calibration. A write to
"Headset Volume" from the audio HAL or tinymix still replaces it, as
before.

Idea from the MTKAnalogAudioFix write-up for MT6789 devices (a
userspace tinymix daemon); this is a separate kernel-side fix.
---
 sound/soc/codecs/mt6358.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/mt6358.c b/sound/soc/codecs/mt6358.c
index 2e0f61d..38657fb 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/mt6358.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/mt6358.c
@@ -6695,6 +6695,16 @@ static int mt6358_codec_probe(struct snd_soc_component *cmpnt)
 				       ARRAY_SIZE(mt6358_snd_vow_controls));
 	mt6358_codec_init_reg(priv);
 
+	/*
+	 * SableOS: start the headphone amp at the stock calibration, -1 dB
+	 * (index 9), instead of the zeroed +8 dB. The stock firmware sets
+	 * "Headset Volume" to 9 9 for every headphone stream; on SableOS
+	 * nothing does, so each power-up ramped the amp to +8 dB and the
+	 * 3.5 mm jack hissed. A later write to the control still wins.
+	 */
+	priv->ana_gain[AUDIO_ANALOG_VOLUME_HPOUTL] = DL_GAIN_N_1DB;
+	priv->ana_gain[AUDIO_ANALOG_VOLUME_HPOUTR] = DL_GAIN_N_1DB;
+
 #if !defined(SKIP_SB) && !defined(CONFIG_FPGA_EARLY_PORTING)
 	priv->hp_current_calibrate_val = get_hp_current_calibrate_val(priv);
 #else
